@startuml

title US13 - List Employees by Role\nDomain Model (DM)

' =====================================================
' Visual configuration
' =====================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9E6
skinparam linetype ortho

hide methods
hide circle

' =====================================================
' Domain concepts
' =====================================================

class Administrator

class Employee {
    ID
    name
}

class Role {
    name
}

' =====================================================
' Domain relationships
' =====================================================

Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" Employee : consults >

Employee "0..*" -- "1" Role : is assigned to >

' =====================================================
' Business rules and constraints
' =====================================================

note right of Employee
Each employee is identified
by an ID and has a name.

Employees can be consulted
according to their assigned role.

A consultation does not modify
employee information.
end note

note right of Role
Represents an employee's
assigned professional role.

Several employees may
share the same role.

Each employee has one
assigned role in the
current US13 model.
end note

note bottom of Administrator
US13 - List Employees by Role

The Administrator selects a role
to consult matching employees.

The consultation returns all
employees assigned to that role.

If no employees match,
an empty result is returned.
end note

note bottom of Role
Examples of roles identified
in the global Domain Model:

Receptionist
MedicalLabTechnician
ClinicalChemistryTechnologist
SpecialistDoctor
Courier

The accepted role values
must be confirmed with
the project requirements.
end note

' =====================================================
' Alignment with existing diagrams
' =====================================================

legend bottom
    US13 - Domain Model

    Employee:
    Business concept represented by
    the Employee class in the CD.

    Role:
    Conceptual representation of the
    role attribute stored in Employee.

    Administrator:
    Primary actor represented in
    the SSD and SD.

    Technical components such as
    EmployeeRepository and
    ListEmployeesByRole are
    intentionally excluded.
endlegend

@enduml